## Airline Reservation Systems

### Use Case: Flight Booking System

**Scenario:** Customer booking flight and seat reservation

```
Reservation Flow:
1. Customer searches available flights
2. Selects flight and seats
3. CICS validates availability (lock seats)
4. Payment processing
5. Confirm booking
6. Send confirmation
7. Release locks
```

### Theory: Deadlock Prevention

```
Problem: Multiple users booking same seat simultaneously

┌─ User A wants: Seat 12A on Flight AA100
│
├─ User B wants: Seat 12B on Flight AA100
│  (Both involve same flight, different seats)
│
└─ Can cause deadlock if not managed

CICS Solution:
├─ Lock at flight level (not seat)
├─ Process one booking at a time
├─ Release lock immediately
├─ Timeout detection (5 seconds)
└─ Automatic abort if timeout
```

### Code Example: Seat Reservation

```cobol
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. FLIGHT-BOOKING.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-FLIGHT-ID         PIC 9(5).
01 WS-SEAT-NUMBER       PIC X(3).
01 WS-CUSTOMER-ID       PIC 9(8).
01 WS-BOOKING-REF       PIC X(10).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.

BOOK-FLIGHT.
    PERFORM GET-BOOKING-REQUEST.
    PERFORM LOCK-FLIGHT-SEATS.
    PERFORM VALIDATE-SEAT-AVAILABLE.
    PERFORM PROCESS-PAYMENT.
    PERFORM CREATE-BOOKING.
    PERFORM UPDATE-SEAT-STATUS.
    PERFORM UNLOCK-FLIGHT-SEATS.
    PERFORM SEND-CONFIRMATION.
    STOP RUN.

GET-BOOKING-REQUEST.
    EXEC CICS RECEIVE MAP('BOOKMAP')
        MAPSET('BOOKSET')
        INTO(BOOKING-REQUEST)
    END-EXEC.
    
    MOVE FLIGHT-ID TO WS-FLIGHT-ID.
    MOVE SEAT-NUM TO WS-SEAT-NUMBER.
    MOVE CUST-ID TO WS-CUSTOMER-ID.

LOCK-FLIGHT-SEATS.
    * Read flight record with exclusive lock
    EXEC CICS READ
        DATASET('FLIGHTS')
        INTO(FLIGHT-RECORD)
        RIDFLD(WS-FLIGHT-ID)
        EXCLUSIVE
        WAIT
        RESP(WS-RESP)
        NOTOPEN
            PERFORM FLIGHT-NOT-AVAILABLE
        END-NOTOPEN
        NOTFND
            PERFORM FLIGHT-NOT-FOUND
        END-NOTFND
    END-EXEC.

VALIDATE-SEAT-AVAILABLE.
    * Check if seat is available
    IF SEAT-STATUS(WS-SEAT-NUMBER) NOT = 'A'
        MOVE 'Seat not available' TO ERROR-MSG
        PERFORM UNLOCK-AND-FAIL
    END-IF.

PROCESS-PAYMENT.
    MOVE 'PROCESS' TO PAYMENT-FUNCTION.
    EXEC CICS LINK
        PROGRAM('PAYMENT-SERVICE')
        COMMAREA(PAYMENT-AREA)
        LENGTH(PAYMENT-LENGTH)
    END-EXEC.
    
    IF PAYMENT-STATUS NOT = 'SUCCESS'
        MOVE 'Payment failed' TO ERROR-MSG
        PERFORM UNLOCK-AND-FAIL
    END-IF.

CREATE-BOOKING.
    * Generate booking reference
    EXEC CICS LINK
        PROGRAM('GEN-BOOKING-REF')
        COMMAREA(BOOKING-REF-AREA)
        LENGTH(REF-LENGTH)
    END-EXEC.
    
    MOVE GENERATED-REF TO WS-BOOKING-REF.
    
    * Write booking record
    EXEC CICS WRITE
        DATASET('BOOKINGS')
        FROM(BOOKING-RECORD)
        RIDFLD(WS-BOOKING-REF)
    END-EXEC.

UPDATE-SEAT-STATUS.
    * Mark seat as booked
    MOVE 'B' TO SEAT-STATUS(WS-SEAT-NUMBER).
    MOVE WS-CUSTOMER-ID TO SEAT-CUSTOMER(WS-SEAT-NUMBER).
    
    * Update flight record
    EXEC CICS UPDATE
        DATASET('FLIGHTS')
        FROM(FLIGHT-RECORD)
        RIDFLD(WS-FLIGHT-ID)
    END-EXEC.
    
    * Commit all changes
    EXEC CICS SYNCPOINT
    END-EXEC.

UNLOCK-FLIGHT-SEATS.
    * Lock is automatically released
    * No explicit unlock needed in CICS
    * Released at transaction end
    CONTINUE.

SEND-CONFIRMATION.
    MOVE WS-BOOKING-REF TO CONF-BOOKING-REF.
    MOVE CURRENT-DATE TO CONF-DATE.
    MOVE CURRENT-TIME TO CONF-TIME.
    
    EXEC CICS SEND MAP('CONFIRMMAP')
        MAPSET('BOOKSET')
        FROM(CONFIRMATION-AREA)
        ERASE
    END-EXEC.
    
    EXEC CICS RETURN
    END-EXEC.

UNLOCK-AND-FAIL.
    * Automatic rollback releases locks
    EXEC CICS ROLLBACK
    END-EXEC.
    EXEC CICS SEND TEXT
        FROM(ERROR-MSG)
        LENGTH(50)
        ERASE
    END-EXEC.
    EXEC CICS RETURN
    END-EXEC.

FLIGHT-NOT-AVAILABLE.
    MOVE 'Flight not available for booking' TO ERROR-MSG.
    PERFORM UNLOCK-AND-FAIL.

FLIGHT-NOT-FOUND.
    MOVE 'Flight not found' TO ERROR-MSG.
    PERFORM UNLOCK-AND-FAIL.
```

