## Retail & E-Commerce

### Use Case: Point of Sale System

**Scenario:** Customer checkout at retail store

```
POS Workflow:
1. Scan products (barcode)
2. Calculate subtotal
3. Apply discounts/coupons
4. Collect payment
5. Process payment
6. Generate receipt
7. Update inventory
8. Complete transaction
```

### Code Example: Inventory Update

```cobol
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. POS-CHECKOUT.

DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01 WS-PRODUCT-ID        PIC X(20).
01 WS-QUANTITY          PIC 9(4).
01 WS-PRICE             PIC 9(7)V99.
01 WS-TOTAL             PIC 9(9)V99.
01 WS-TRANSACTION-ID    PIC X(10).

PROCEDURE DIVISION.

PROCESS-SALE.
    PERFORM SCAN-PRODUCTS.
    PERFORM CALCULATE-TOTAL.
    PERFORM COLLECT-PAYMENT.
    PERFORM UPDATE-INVENTORY.
    PERFORM PRINT-RECEIPT.
    PERFORM RECORD-SALE.
    STOP RUN.

SCAN-PRODUCTS.
    PERFORM UNTIL NO-MORE-PRODUCTS
        EXEC CICS RECEIVE
            FROM(BARCODE-INPUT)
        END-EXEC
        
        * Lookup product
        EXEC CICS READ
            DATASET('PRODUCTS')
            INTO(PRODUCT-RECORD)
            RIDFLD(WS-PRODUCT-ID)
        END-EXEC
        
        * Add to cart
        PERFORM ADD-TO-CART
    END-PERFORM.

UPDATE-INVENTORY.
    PERFORM VARYING ITEM-INDEX 
            FROM 1 BY 1 
            UNTIL ITEM-INDEX > ITEMS-COUNT
        
        MOVE ITEM-ID(ITEM-INDEX) TO WS-PRODUCT-ID
        MOVE ITEM-QTY(ITEM-INDEX) TO WS-QUANTITY
        
        * Read inventory
        EXEC CICS READ
            DATASET('INVENTORY')
            INTO(INVENTORY-RECORD)
            RIDFLD(WS-PRODUCT-ID)
            EXCLUSIVE
        END-EXEC
        
        * Reduce quantity
        SUBTRACT WS-QUANTITY FROM INVENTORY-QTY
        
        * Check for low stock
        IF INVENTORY-QTY < REORDER-LEVEL
            PERFORM TRIGGER-REORDER
        END-IF
        
        * Update record
        EXEC CICS UPDATE
            DATASET('INVENTORY')
            FROM(INVENTORY-RECORD)
            RIDFLD(WS-PRODUCT-ID)
        END-EXEC
    END-PERFORM.
    
    * Commit all inventory updates
    EXEC CICS SYNCPOINT
    END-EXEC.
```

