## Common Pitfalls

### Pitfall 1: Not Using SYNCPOINT

```cobol
* WRONG: Changes might not be committed
EXEC CICS UPDATE
    DATASET('ACCOUNTS')
    FROM(ACCOUNT-RECORD)
    RIDFLD(ACCOUNT-ID)
END-EXEC.

EXEC CICS RETURN
    TRANSID('NEXT')
END-EXEC.

* CORRECT: Explicitly commit
EXEC CICS UPDATE
    DATASET('ACCOUNTS')
    FROM(ACCOUNT-RECORD)
    RIDFLD(ACCOUNT-ID)
END-EXEC.

EXEC CICS SYNCPOINT
END-EXEC.

EXEC CICS RETURN
    TRANSID('NEXT')
END-EXEC.
```

### Pitfall 2: Blocking on I/O

```cobol
* WRONG: Holding user session during processing
PERFORM VARYING I 1 BY 1 UNTIL I > 1000
    * Time-consuming processing
    PERFORM HEAVY-CALCULATION
END-PERFORM.

* CORRECT: Return quickly, queue processing
EXEC CICS PUT QUEUE('PROC-QUEUE')
    FROM(PROCESSING-ITEM)
    LENGTH(ITEM-LENGTH)
END-EXEC.

EXEC CICS RETURN
    TRANSID('RESULT')
END-EXEC.

* Separate batch job processes queue
```

### Pitfall 3: Holding Locks Too Long

```cobol
* WRONG: Unnecessary lock hold
EXEC CICS READ
    DATASET('MASTER')
    INTO(MASTER-RECORD)
    RIDFLD(MASTER-KEY)
    EXCLUSIVE
END-EXEC.

* Long processing time
PERFORM VALIDATION.
PERFORM FORMATTING.
PERFORM CALCULATIONS.

* Lock released only at SYNCPOINT
EXEC CICS SYNCPOINT
END-EXEC.

* CORRECT: Minimize lock duration
EXEC CICS READ
    DATASET('MASTER')
    INTO(MASTER-RECORD)
    RIDFLD(MASTER-KEY)
END-EXEC.

* Non-exclusive lock, can read locally
PERFORM VALIDATION.
PERFORM FORMATTING.
PERFORM CALCULATIONS.

* Only lock for update
EXEC CICS READ
    DATASET('MASTER')
    INTO(MASTER-RECORD)
    RIDFLD(MASTER-KEY)
    EXCLUSIVE
END-EXEC.

PERFORM UPDATE-RECORD.

EXEC CICS SYNCPOINT
END-EXEC.
```

